# Dependencies
node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.js

# Build outputs
dist/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo


# Convex
.convex/
# packages/convex/convex/_generated is committed (see api.d.ts header)

# OMO planning workspace (evidence artifacts only — plans and drafts are tracked)
# Must exclude the CONTENTS, not the directory: git does not descend into an
# excluded directory, so `.omo/evidence/` would make the negation below
# unreachable.
.omo/evidence/*
# Exception: the device notification baseline. Later work adds a second
# delivery Tier (ADR 0003) and must be diffed against a known-good starting
# point, so this artifact has to exist in a clean checkout rather than only on
# the machine that produced it. Everything else under evidence/ stays ignored.
!.omo/evidence/issue-5-baseline-all-cases.json
# Exception: the write-path cutover run diffed against that baseline. Tracked
# for the same reason and by the same rule — `docs/poc-results.md` cites it as
# the evidence closing issue #6, and a citation to a file that exists only on
# one machine is not evidence. The three per-pass reports it was merged from
# stay ignored: this one records which pass evaluated each case, so they add
# nothing a clean checkout needs.
!.omo/evidence/issue-6-cutover-verification.json
# Exception: the legacy-deletion run, 7/7 merged from three passes and diffed
# against the #5 baseline. Same rule again — it closes issue #8's device
# criterion and records which pass evaluated each case, so the three per-pass
# reports it merges stay ignored.
!.omo/evidence/issue-8-legacy-deletion-verification.json
# Exception: the issue #7 round trip. Not a harness report — a hand-driven
# create/push/wipe/pull across two installs on one account, recording what the
# Convex documents and the device's own SQLite rows held at each step. Tracked
# because it is the only evidence that the pull path works on a real device,
# and because its `not_verified` list is the honest boundary of that claim.
!.omo/evidence/issue-7-round-trip-verification.json
# Exception: case 12, the run proving the app asks for POST_NOTIFICATIONS and
# then actually delivers. Same rule — `docs/poc-results.md` cites it as what
# closes issue #20, the most consequential defect this project has shipped, and
# a citation to a file on one machine is not evidence. Worth more than most:
# the same case was also run against a build that never asks and recorded the
# FAIL, so this artifact is a verdict from an instrument known to be able to
# return the other answer.
!.omo/evidence/issue-20-case-12-permission.json

